<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="041" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Derive follow-on chips/cards deterministically from mounted parity tools + interaction pattern; per-item→cards, query→chips; collapse card stacks (FR-14)</title>
    <phase>4 — Interaction patterns + accurate follow-ons</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Edits the ConversationPane follow-on/proactive-card surface (.tsx) — the sequential UI spine; element-type correctness per the criteria doc</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified deterministic derivation with an explicit criteria doc (per-item→cards, query→chips); literal execution against ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Wave5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ConversationPane.tsx (the sequential spine — shared with 025/026 per-item cards and 040); coordinate merge order with notification-spine/analysis-hub which also touch this file.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>040</deps>
    <tags>spaarkeai, frontend, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>In ConversationPane.tsx, derive follow-on chips/cards DETERMINISTICALLY from the mounted parity tools + the interaction pattern (task 040) — never model-invented. Apply the element-type rule from docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md: per-item actions on an active item render as CARDS; overview/query turn-follow-ons render as CHIPS. Collapse proactive card STACKS behind ONE disclosure header. No follow-on may reference an unmounted tool.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React/TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 expertise on the SpaarkeAi ConversationPane; comfortable applying the Assistant UI element criteria (bubble/chip/card/tab).</role>
  <goal>Follow-ons for an open tab correspond exactly to that widget's mounted parity tools + declared pattern; none reference an unmounted tool; per-item actions render as cards and query follow-ons as chips; multiple proactive cards collapse under one disclosure header.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-14 — deterministic follow-ons + element type. The model must NOT invent follow-ons. This task derives them deterministically from (a) the mounted parity tools for the open tab (task 030 pre-filter output) and (b) the widget's interaction pattern field (task 040). Element type follows docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md: per-item actions on an active item → CARDS (persistent act-on items — email Reply/Reply All/Forward/Summarize; document Summarize/Draft-response/Draft-memo); overview/query turn-follow-ons → CHIPS (throwaway next-questions after a chat answer). Proactive card stacks collapse behind ONE disclosure header (criteria doc + design A4). Edits land in ConversationPane.tsx — the proactive-card surface (~:164-167) and the follow-on renderer. ConversationPane is a sequential spine shared with 025/026 (per-item cards) — coordinate.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (proactive-card surface ~:164-167; follow-on derivation + renderer)</file>
      <file>the mounted parity tools for the open tab (task 030 pre-filter output) — the deterministic source of follow-ons</file>
      <file>the interaction-pattern registration field (task 040) — respond/direct/hybrid</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md (bubble vs chip vs card vs tab decision + collapse rule)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="follow-on derivation">Follow-ons are derived deterministically from mounted tools + the pattern field — MUST NOT be invented by the model or produced by a classifier.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA" scope="element type">Per-item actions on an active item → CARDS; overview/query turn-follow-ons → CHIPS. No code/keys in chip/card labels; hover only on clickable regions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA" scope="proactive card stacks">Multiple proactive cards collapse behind ONE disclosure header.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-047" scope="the card surface">The reactive/local-selection card surface stays distinct from the server-initiated notification spine (NFR-07) — no merge, no new push channel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="tool references">No follow-on may reference an unmounted tool (must reflect the current pre-filter projection).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the current proactive-card surface + follow-on renderer in ConversationPane.tsx and the element criteria doc.</step>
    <step order="2">Build the deterministic derivation: for the open tab, map its mounted parity tools + interaction pattern to a follow-on set.</step>
    <step order="3">Select element type: per-item actions on an active item → cards; overview/query turn-follow-ons → chips.</step>
    <step order="4">Collapse multiple proactive cards behind one disclosure header.</step>
    <step order="5">Guard: no follow-on references an unmounted tool (reflect the current projection).</step>
    <step order="6">Add UI tests (see ui-tests) covering the correspondence, element type, and collapse.</step>
    <step order="7">Build the SpaarkeAi package; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <ui-tests>
    <test>With the Email tab open + an email selected, per-item follow-ons render as CARDS matching the mounted email tools (Reply/Reply All/Forward/Summarize); none reference an unmounted tool.</test>
    <test>After an overview/query chat answer, turn-follow-ons render as CHIPS (not cards).</test>
    <test>With multiple proactive cards present, they collapse behind ONE disclosure header (expand reveals the stack).</test>
    <test>Closing a tab removes its follow-ons (they reflect the current pre-filter projection — no stale/unmounted-tool reference).</test>
    <test>No card/chip label contains code or a raw tool key; hover affordance appears only on clickable regions.</test>
  </ui-tests>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a required follow-on cannot be derived deterministically from mounted tools + the pattern field (i.e. it would require the model to invent it), STOP and escalate (ADR-039 / FR-14 bound) rather than emitting a model-invented follow-on.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>The proactive-card surface exists in ConversationPane.tsx (~:164-167) but follow-ons are not deterministically bound to mounted tools + a pattern field, and element-type/collapse rules are not applied.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend the existing card/chip surface with a deterministic derivation keyed off task 030 (mounted tools) + task 040 (pattern); no new surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Follow-ons drift from actual capabilities (reference unmounted tools) or are model-invented; card/chip choice is wrong; proactive stacks clutter the pane (the FR-14 defects).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (deterministic follow-on derivation + element-type + collapse)</output>
    <output type="test">ConversationPane UI tests (correspondence, card vs chip, collapse)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Follow-ons for an open tab correspond exactly to that widget's mounted parity tools + declared pattern.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No follow-on references an unmounted tool (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-item actions on an active item render as cards; overview/query follow-ons render as chips.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Multiple proactive cards collapse under one disclosure header.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Follow-ons are deterministic — not model-invented (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The reactive card surface stays distinct from the ADR-047 spine (no push channel added).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UI tests added and pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Depends on task 040 (interaction-pattern field) and reflects task 030's mounted-tool projection. ConversationPane is the sequential spine (shared with 025/026) — coordinate merge order with notification-spine/analysis-hub; /conflict-check before the PR.</notes>
  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files in knowledge/files. Follow task-execute skill.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
